        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Daily transits at 6&ndash;12 vessels/day against a 50/day threshold &mdash; 10&ndash;24% of threshold. Lloyd&rsquo;s war-risk premiums at ~2.5% of hull (above 1.5% indicator). No major shipping line announcement. Trump-Xi summit (May 14&ndash;15) is the key near-term pivot: a named Chinese commitment on Hormuz would materially shift this probability, but no such commitment issued at publication. A YES by June 10 requires a near-linear chain from Chinese commitment through Iranian compliance, Lloyd&rsquo;s re-rating, and major carrier return.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Hormuz Strait Monitor (or UNCTAD, or Lloyd&rsquo;s List) reports &ge;50 daily transits averaged over 7 consecutive days within the horizon window.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Hormuz Strait Monitor (primary), Lloyd&rsquo;s List Intelligence (secondary), UNCTAD Maritime Trade (lagging).</dd>
